@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/auth

### 1. Iniciar sesión antes de activar (debe fallar con 403 Forbidden)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Activar cuenta con datos de identidad incorrectos (debe fallar con error genérico 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/activate-account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
  "name": "Juan",
  "surname": "Pérez",
  "docNumber": "99999999",
  "newPassword": "miPasswordSeguro123"
}

### 3. Activar cuenta con email inexistente (debe fallar con el MISMO error genérico 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/activate-account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noexiste@example.com",
  "name": "Juan",
  "surname": "Pérez",
  "docNumber": "30111222",
  "newPassword": "miPasswordSeguro123"
}

### 4. Activar cuenta exitosa (Socio Juan Pérez - DNI 30111222)
POST {{baseUrl}}/activate-account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
  "name": "Juan",
  "surname": "Pérez",
  "docNumber": "30111222",
  "newPassword": "miPasswordSeguro123"
}

### 5. Reintentar activar cuenta ya activada (debe fallar con 400: Account already activated)
POST {{baseUrl}}/activate-account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
  "name": "Juan",
  "surname": "Pérez",
  "docNumber": "30111222",
  "newPassword": "miPasswordSeguro123"
}

### 6. Iniciar sesión con contraseña incorrecta (401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
  "password": "passwordIncorrecto"
}

### 7. Iniciar sesión exitoso (Socio activado)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "juan.perez@example.com",
  "password": "miPasswordSeguro123"
}

### 8. Iniciar sesión como Administrador (admin@gym.com / admin1234)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@gym.com",
  "password": "admin1234"
}

